  "reveal": {
    "ledger_voiced": "From my book. The sitting ran as I ran it: the whispered voice: a thrown voice; the cold draught: a phial of scent; the spirit writing: a changed slate; the table's tilt: a trimmed wick; the raps: the wedge of a boot; the spirit trumpet: the window cord. The scent of violets I did not produce, and did not care for.\n\nAs to the evening's business: the account Dr Tobias Quill swore to was an invention, for those hands were out of the dark and about their own work. Effie Strange was past any sitting's reach before the lamps were lit.\n\nThe dead say what it profits me they say; on this occasion they profited Dr Tobias Quill more.",
